A||N||3||SloPonti||HOW DO I TIME MY FOUR BANGER???||||5||
Z||000000||SloPonti||02-04-2000||09:14 PM||||i got the motor back into the car and it is running great! now all i need to do is get the timing perfect on it! like i said it is running but i just can't seem to get the timing right but i am doing it by ear! i know that it is suppose to be 8 degrees but just don't know how to get it there! how do i time it using a timing light? isn't there something i have to ground out or diconnect something! or maybe i am totally off here! so if anyone could give me step by step instuctions-it would be of great help-the car is an 84 four cylinder!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||02-04-2000||09:25 PM||||There is a sticker on the bottom of the engine lid that will tell you if you need to ground out the ALDL (A&B terminal) connector to get the engine in base timing mode. I'm not shore if this procedure needs to be done on the four because the one I have is an 87 with the distributorless ignition.  You have to put the v6 Fiero in base timing mode and most other GM vehicles to set the base timing thou. To ground out the ALDL connector use a paper clip and insert it in the A and B terminals with the engine off. Start the engine and set your timing like you normally would do. Shut the engine off and pull out the paper clip and you are done. When the computer is in Base timing mode the check engine light will be flashing, and the engine will run like crap, this is normal.<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 02-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||02-05-2000||01:37 AM||||He's right... I've time both Fiero's like that.   If you don't jumper those two together, you'll get a totally messed up reading.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SloPonti||02-05-2000||02:26 PM||||thanks guys-what you said worked and the new motor is now running great!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||10
